  "question": {
    "text": "The set of points on the axis of the parabola <math><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> from which all the three normals drawn to the parabola are real and distinct, is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mo>{</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>}</mo></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mo>{</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>}</mo></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mo>{</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>}</mo></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mo>{</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>}</mo></math>",
