  "solution": {
    "text": "Given equation of the parabola can be rewritten as<br /><br /><math><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math><br /><br />Axis of the parabola is <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>,<br />equation of normal is<br /><br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br />Let <math><mo>(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math> is a point on its axis, then<br /><br /><math><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>3</mn></math> for real &amp; distinct values of <math><mi>m</mi></math>"
  }
}